  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Trumps**: The higher end of the turn-up tile is the trump suit. 2. **The Miss (Widow)**: In 3-4 player games, an extra hand of 5 tiles is dealt. Players can swap their hand for 'The Miss' or drop out. 3. **Dealer's Swap**: If the dealer keeps their hand, they can swap one tile for the turn-up trump tile. 4. **Trick Play**: Lead any tile. Must follow suit (if lead is a 5-2, the suit is 5). If unable to follow, must play a trump if held.",
    Player: "1. **Trumps**: The higher end of the turn-up tile is the trump suit. 2. **The Miss (Widow)**: In 3-4 player games, an extra hand of 5 tiles is dealt. Players can swap their hand for 'The Miss' or drop out. 3. **Dealer's Swap**: If the dealer keeps their hand, they can swap one tile for the turn-up trump tile. 4. **Trick Play**: Lead any tile. Must follow suit (if lead is a 5-2, the suit is 5). If unable to follow, must play a trump if held.",
    objective: "Win as many tricks as possible to take a share of the pool. Avoid being 'Looed' (taking zero tricks).",
    gameplay: "1. **Trumps**: The higher end of the turn-up tile is the trump suit. 2. **The Miss (Widow)**: In 3-4 player games, an extra hand of 5 tiles is dealt. Players can swap their hand for 'The Miss' or drop out. 3. **Dealer's Swap**: If the dealer keeps their hand, they can swap one tile for the turn-up trump tile. 4. **Trick Play**: Lead any tile. Must follow suit (if lead is a 5-2, the suit is 5). If unable to follow, must play a trump if held.",
    keyRules: [
      'Suit of a tile is determined by its ends. A 5-2 belongs to suit 5 and suit 2.',
      'Trumps always beat non-trump suits.',
      'Only the first/second players to opt in can take the Miss.',
      'Each trick won earns 1/5 of the pool.',
      "Player who takes no tricks is 'Looed' and must pay penalty equal to original pool amount.",
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
