    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 5 card(s) per player.',
      "Rule example: Win as many tricks as possible to take a share of the pool. Avoid being 'Looed' (taking zero tricks).",
      "Turn-flow example: 1. **Trumps**: The higher end of the turn-up tile is the trump suit. 2. **The Miss (Widow)**: In 3-4 player games, an extra hand of 5 tiles is dealt. Players can swap their hand for 'The Miss' or drop out. 3. **Dealer's Swap**: If the dealer keeps their hand, they can swap one tile for the turn-up trump tile. 4. **Trick Play**: Lead any tile. Must follow suit (if lead is a 5-2, the suit is 5). If unable to follow, must play a trump if held.",
      'Scoring example: Each trick earns a share of the pool; taking zero tricks triggers Loo penalty. Best net gain over agreed session length wins..',
